.TH TOMESH 1
.SH NAME
tomesh \- write the triangles of parts as an OBJ mesh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tomesh
[
.B \-c
.I chord
] [
.B \-a
.I deg
] [
.B \-n
]
.IR stream.st | \-
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tomesh
writes each part of a stream
.RI ( stream (5))
as an object of a Wavefront OBJ file on the standard output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
o NAME
# color R G B
v X Y Z
vn X Y Z
f A B C
.fi
.RE
.PP
The color is that of the material of a placed part, from 0 to 1.
Vertices are in world mm, numbered from 1 through the file;
triangles are counterclockwise seen from outside.
Each mesh is closed (faces share the points of their edges).
The triangles of a part with coats
.RI ( sm (5))
are cut along the coats, and those of each material of a coat, or of
the finish of faces of a solid
.RI ( part (5)),
come after the rest in a group of their own: a line
.BI usemtl " material" ,
the comment
.BI "# color" " r g b"
if the stream gives the material, that of the body, 0.85 of it, for a
texture, and the faces.
A texture comes after the usemtl line as the comment
.BI "# texture " grade ,
its grade of VDI 3400, or 30 for a texture of a callout alone, which
.IR view (1)
draws as a grain.
.TP
.BI \-c " chord"
Keep every triangle within
.I chord
mm of its face (default 0.02).
.TP
.BI \-a " deg"
Let no triangle turn more than
.I deg
degrees (default 10).
.TP
.B \-n
Write vertex normals, with faces as
.IB a // n .
.SH SEE ALSO
stream(5), part(5), view(1)
